Package: laridae
Type: Package
Title: Constrained Triangulation and Meshing with CGAL
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Michael D.", "Sumner", , "mdsumner@gmail.com", c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mark", "Padgham", role = "ctb"))
Description: A persistent constrained Delaunay triangulation handle backed by
    CGAL's 'Constrained_triangulation_plus_2' and 'Delaunay_mesher_2'. Points
    and constraint segments can be inserted and removed at any time, crossing
    constraints are resolved by inserting the crossing, and the mesh can be
    refined by minimum angle, maximum area, or a sizing field that varies
    with position. Input and output follow the vertices / segments /
    triangles contract shared with 'cdtr', including per-triangle constraint
    depth.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
LinkingTo: cpp11
SystemRequirements: CGAL (>= 6.0) headers, Boost headers, C++17
Suggests:
    bench,
    sf,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
URL: https://github.com/hypertidy/laridae
BugReports: https://github.com/hypertidy/laridae/issues
